cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these courses, or material taken from them, please cite them as below."
title: "Self-study courses: combinatorial & constrained optimization, and mechanics to relativity"
abstract: >-
  Two independent self-study curricula sharing one repository and one deployment.
  Combinatorial & constrained optimization is 32 units in which theory is interleaved
  with from-scratch Python implementations, each then benchmarked against the industrial
  solver that does the same job; its labs, tests and reference solutions are in this
  repository but deliberately not on the published site. Mechanics to relativity is 41
  units from Newton's second law to Einstein's field equations, in which every piece of
  mathematics arrives only at the moment a physical problem stalls without it; it is
  worked on paper, and is published whole, hint ladders and worked solutions included.
